              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon and shield. May have throwing spear (+2 pts). May replace shield with additional hand weapon (+3 pts) or double-handed axe (+3 pts). Berserkers: a unit of Hirdmen can contain up to three Berserkers, placed with the unit at the start of the battle (not hidden; represented by a ferocious model in the front rank). Take at most one Berserker group per unit of Hirdmen. (Shieldwall p.13)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="0045-b546-2237-7303" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
